  <h2>7 Exercises To Do Every Day</h2>
  <p>A simple daily routine that takes 10-15 minutes and provides consistent full-body activation:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>March in place</strong> (1 minute) - Warm-up, ankle mobility</li>
    <li><strong>Bodyweight squats</strong> (10-15 reps) - Legs, glutes, core</li>
    <li><strong>Push-ups</strong> (5-8 reps, modify as needed) - Chest, shoulders, arms</li>
    <li><strong>Glute bridges</strong> (15 reps) - Glutes, hamstrings, core</li>
    <li><strong>Plank</strong> (30-45 seconds) - Core, shoulders, back</li>
    <li><strong>Lunges</strong> (10 each leg) - Legs, balance, stability</li>
    <li><strong>Jumping jacks</strong> (30 seconds) - Cardio boost, full body</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Full Body Workout At Home Without Equipment</h2>
  <p>You can build significant fitness using only bodyweight. Focus on these principles:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Increase time under tension</strong> - Slow down each rep for more challenge</li>
    <li><strong>Reduce rest periods</strong> - Keep heart rate elevated</li>
    <li><strong>Add isometric holds</strong> - Hold positions at peak contraction</li>
    <li><strong>Combine exercises</strong> - Flow from one movement to the next</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>All In One Exercise Machines For Home</h2>
  <p>While bodyweight exercises are excellent, machines offer progressive resistance and variety. Consider these options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Power towers</strong> - Support pull-ups, dips, and knee raises</li>
    <li><strong>Adjustable benches with rack</strong> - Enable incline/decline movements</li>
    <li><strong>Compact multi-gyms</strong> - Provide multiple exercise stations in one unit</li>
    <li><strong>Kettlebell sets</strong> - Versatile weight for swings, presses, squats</li>
  </ul>

